---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout section="Tokens &amp; JWT" title="Tokens, JWT, Claims &amp; Endpoints">
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <div class="learn-layout">
      <nav class="toc">
        <div class="toc-label">On this page</div>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#token-consumers">Token Types &amp; Consumers</a></li>
          <li><a href="#scopes-vs-claims">Scope vs Claim vs Response Type</a></li>
          <li><a href="#jwt-structure">JWT Structure &amp; Tamper-Proofing</a></li>
          <li><a href="#claims">Standard &amp; Custom Claims</a></li>
          <li><a href="#signing">RS256 vs HS256 Signing</a></li>
          <li><a href="#jwks">JWKS Verification</a></li>
          <li><a href="#endpoints">The Four OAuth Endpoints</a></li>
          <li><a href="#wam">Web Access Management (WAM)</a></li>
        </ul>
        <hr class="toc-divider" />
        <nav class="toc-nav">
          <a href={base + '/oidc'}>&larr; OIDC</a>
          <a href={base + '/api-guide'}>API Guide &rarr;</a>
        </nav>
      </nav>

      <main class="content">
        <div class="page-header">
          <span class="badge badge-advanced">Advanced &middot; 25 min</span>
          <h1>Tokens, JWT, Claims &amp; Endpoints</h1>
          <p class="lead">In-depth guide to token types, JWT validation, cryptographic signature verification (RS256 / JWKS), standard claims, and token introspection / revocation endpoints.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- TOKEN CONSUMERS -->
        <section id="token-consumers">
          <h2>Token Types &amp; Intended Consumers</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Token Type</th><th>Intended Consumer</th><th>Security Purpose &amp; Rule</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Access Token</strong></td>
                <td>Resource Server (API)</td>
                <td>Presented in <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> headers. Grants access to protected endpoints. Never inspect inside client apps.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>ID Token</strong></td>
                <td>Client Application</td>
                <td>Signed JWT proving user authentication. <strong>Never send to backend APIs as Bearer tokens!</strong></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Refresh Token</strong></td>
                <td>Authorization Server</td>
                <td>Long-lived credential used exclusively to fetch fresh access tokens. Stored securely in HTTP-only cookies or secret vaults.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <!-- SCOPES VS CLAIMS -->
        <section id="scopes-vs-claims">
          <h2>Scope vs Claim vs Response Type</h2>
          <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap:1rem; margin:1.5rem 0;">
            <div style="background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); padding:1rem; border-radius:var(--radius);">
              <h3 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">Scope</h3>
              <p>Permissions requested by the client during authorization (e.g. <code>read:reports</code>, <code>openid</code>).</p>
            </div>
            <div style="background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); padding:1rem; border-radius:var(--radius);">
              <h3 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">Claim</h3>
              <p>Key-value assertion packed inside a JWT payload about a user or context (e.g. <code>"sub": "123"</code>, <code>"roles": ["Admin"]</code>).</p>
            </div>
            <div style="background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); padding:1rem; border-radius:var(--radius);">
              <h3 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">Response Type</h3>
              <p>Instructs the Authorization Server what artifacts to return in the front-channel redirect (e.g. <code>code</code>, <code>id_token</code>).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- JWT STRUCTURE -->
        <section id="jwt-structure">
          <h2>JWT Structure &amp; Tamper-Proofing (RFC 7519)</h2>
          <p>A JSON Web Token consists of three base64url-encoded parts separated by periods: <code>header.payload.signature</code></p>
          
          <pre><code><span class="c">// 1. HEADER (Base64URL encoded)</span>
&#123;
  "alg": "RS256",
  "typ": "JWT",
  "kid": "key_2026_01"
&#125;

<span class="c">// 2. PAYLOAD (Base64URL encoded)</span>
&#123;
  "iss": "https://authorization-server.example.com",
  "sub": "usr_445566",
  "aud": "https://api.example.com",
  "exp": 1755003600,
  "iat": 1755000000,
  "roles": ["Manager"]
&#125;

<span class="c">// 3. SIGNATURE</span>
RS256(Base64URL(Header) + "." + Base64URL(Payload), PrivateKey)</code></pre>
          
          <div class="callout tip">
            <strong>🔒 Tamper-Proof Security:</strong> If an attacker modifies even a single character in the Header or Payload, signature verification fails because the attacker lacks the private key.
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- CLAIMS -->
        <section id="claims">
          <h2>Standard JWT Claims (RFC 7519 Section 4.1)</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Claim</th><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>iss</code></td><td>Issuer</td><td>Identifies the Authorization Server that created the token.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>sub</code></td><td>Subject</td><td>Unique identifier of the resource owner / user.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>aud</code></td><td>Audience</td><td>Intended recipient of the token (must match API identifier).</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>exp</code></td><td>Expiration</td><td>Unix timestamp after which the token is invalid.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>nbf</code></td><td>Not Before</td><td>Unix timestamp before which the token must not be accepted.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>iat</code></td><td>Issued At</td><td>Unix timestamp when the token was created.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>jti</code></td><td>JWT ID</td><td>Unique token identifier used to prevent replay attacks.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <!-- SIGNING -->
        <section id="signing">
          <h2>RS256 vs HS256 Signature Verification</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Dimension</th><th>HS256 (Symmetric)</th><th>RS256 (Asymmetric)</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><strong>Key Type</strong></td><td>Single Shared Secret</td><td>Private Key (Signs) + Public Key (Verifies)</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Security Model</strong></td><td>Risky: All APIs need the secret</td><td>Ideal: Only IdP holds private key; APIs verify via public JWKS</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Enterprise Standard</strong></td><td>Internal services only</td><td>Recommended standard for all public &amp; multi-service architectures</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <!-- JWKS -->
        <section id="jwks">
          <h2>JWKS Verification (RFC 7517)</h2>
          <p>Resource servers verify incoming tokens by dynamically retrieving the IdP's public keys from <code>/.well-known/jwks.json</code>:</p>
          <pre><code>GET /.well-known/jwks.json HTTP/1.1
Host: authorization-server.example.com

<span class="c">// Response</span>
&#123;
  "keys": [
    &#123;
      "kty": "RSA",
      "use": "sig",
      "alg": "RS256",
      "kid": "key_2026_01",
      "n": "u1WguZo5WOk5Y...",
      "e": "AQAB"
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>
        </section>

        <!-- ENDPOINTS -->
        <section id="endpoints">
          <h2>The Four OAuth Endpoints</h2>
          
          <h3>1. Token Introspection (RFC 7662)</h3>
          <pre><code>POST /introspect HTTP/1.1
Host: authorization-server.example.com
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: Basic Y2xpZW50X2lkOmNsaWVudF9zZWNyZXQ=

token=2YotnFZFEjr1zCsicMWpAA

<span class="c">// Response</span>
&#123;
  "active": true,
  "scope": "read:reports",
  "client_id": "client_app_123",
  "username": "janedoe",
  "exp": 1755003600
&#125;</code></pre>

          <h3>2. Token Revocation (RFC 7009)</h3>
          <pre><code>POST /revoke HTTP/1.1
Host: authorization-server.example.com
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

token=8xLOxBtZp8&amp;token_type_hint=refresh_token</code></pre>
        </section>

        <!-- WAM -->
        <section id="wam">
          <h2>Web Access Management (WAM) Policies</h2>
          <p>Modern Web Access Management engines evaluate token claims and environmental signals in real time before granting access to sensitive business operations:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>User Context:</strong> Evaluates <code>sub</code>, <code>roles</code>, and <code>permissions</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Resource Context:</strong> Evaluates the requested URI (e.g. <code>/api/protected/audit</code>) and HTTP verb (<code>DELETE</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Risk Signals:</strong> IP geolocation, device health compliance, and MFA assurance levels (<code>acr</code> / <code>amr</code>).</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <footer class="page-footer">
          <div class="prev-next">
            <a href={base + '/oidc'}>&larr; OIDC</a>
            <a href={base + '/api-guide'}>Next: API Guide &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </footer>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
